# openclaw stack — manual setup

## Bootstrap env file

```bash
cp openclaw.example openclaw.env
```

Generate a gateway token and fill in `OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN`:

```bash
openssl rand -hex 32
```

Also set at least one model provider key (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is the
default slot in the template). Leave channel tokens commented out for now —
they can be added later either in `openclaw.env` or interactively via the
CLI (see "Add a channel" below).

## First run

```bash
mkdir -p ~/storage/homelab/homelab-conf/openclaw/{state,auth-secrets}
mkdir -p ~/storage/homelab/homelab-data/openclaw/workspace
cd ~/homelab/containers
./up-all-stacks.sh openclaw
```

Check it comes up healthy:

```bash
docker compose -f openclaw/docker-compose.yml ps
docker compose -f openclaw/docker-compose.yml logs -f openclaw-gateway
```

## Reverse proxy (nginx-proxy-manager)

Add a proxy host in the NPM admin UI (see
`containers/nginx-proxy-manager/.setup` for how to reach it):

- Domain: `openclaw.yggdrasil.cfd`
- Forward to: `openclaw_gateway:18789`
- Scheme: `http`
- **Websockets Support: on** — the control UI and agent RPC are websocket
  traffic on the same port as the HTTP API.
- Request a new SSL certificate (HTTP-01, same as every other proxy host)

## Onboarding (model + dashboard)

The web dashboard is the easiest path for a Docker deployment (rather than
the native `openclaw onboard` wizard). From `containers/openclaw/`:

```bash
docker compose --profile cli run --rm openclaw-cli dashboard --no-open
```

This prints a dashboard URL/link. Once the NPM proxy host above is live,
open `https://openclaw.yggdrasil.cfd`, and when prompted for
auth paste in `OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN` from `openclaw.env`. Finish the
setup flow there (confirm model provider, review default agent settings).

## Add a channel (e.g. Telegram)

Get a bot token from the relevant platform first (BotFather for Telegram,
etc.), then either drop it in `openclaw.env` as `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=...`
and restart the gateway, or add it live without restarting:

```bash
docker compose --profile cli run --rm openclaw-cli \
  channels add --channel telegram --token "<token>"
```

## Sanity check

```bash
docker compose exec openclaw-gateway wget -qO- http://127.0.0.1:18789/healthz
```

(No host port is published, so `healthz`/`readyz` are only reachable from
inside the stack's network namespace or through the NPM domain — that's
intentional, matching every other HTTP-facing stack in this repo.)
